{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"DECISION 2 - CARBON CE ARTIFACT: KEEP THE FULL-TEAM RUN (r1). Executed and unchanged, but now on four converging lines of evidence rather than two. A targeted test was added: for each rebar finding, is it matched in the contaminated run but in NEITHER clean run? Persona loss cannot explain such a hit because the two clean runs lose DIFFERENT personas and together cover all six. Result: zero. Two apparent hits at a loose threshold both concern the Lit context file location, and direct inspection shows all three CE runs independently raise that issue in their own wording - it is a four-arm convergent finding, not a transfer. The full evidence set is now: CE detected the stray cache and abstained, self-reported; aggregate lexical overlap with rebar 0.090 contaminated versus 0.076 clean, within noise; zero rebar-unique findings in the contaminated run; and a structural argument previously underweighted - the scoring unit is DISTINCT ISSUES, and copied findings are linked as same_issue in adjudication, so copying could not inflate a distinct-issue count even if it had occurred. Against that, the alternative is certain: both clean-tree attempts lost a persona, and the study's own rule holds that an incomplete team understates CE and therefore FLATTERS rebar, the direction this study must not drift. A fourth attempt was declined to honour the stopping rule fixed before the third, since re-rolling until the process succeeds after seeing three outcomes is a forking path. All three attempts are preserved."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789449255416015001,"uuid":"9f0ea9f8-ffbd-4911-bacc-ebd2421525bd"}